issue.body:
Seeing some IR from #10903 where we're doing an alloc+fill+await (after lots of optimizations).
That's silly... it's sillier to be returning scalar tensors to calling applications but we could probably do something better here.

Stream IR (after IPO, which allows us to see this is a constant):
```mlir
func.func @silly() -> !hal.buffer_view {
  %c4 = arith.constant 4 : index
  %c1065353216_i32 = arith.constant 1065353216 : i32
  %0 = stream.async.splat %c1065353216_i32 : i32 -> !stream.resource<*>{%c4}
  %52 = stream.async.transfer %0 : !stream.resource<*>{%c4} -> !stream.resource<external>{%c4}
  %53 = stream.tensor.export %52 : tensor<f32> in !stream.resource<external>{%c4} -> !hal.buffer_view
  return %53 : !hal.buffer_view
}
```

This gets lowered into an alloc and fill:
```mlir
func.func @silly() -> !hal.buffer_view {
  %c4 = arith.constant 4 : index
  %c1065353216_i32 = arith.constant 1065353216 : i32
  %13 = stream.resource.alloc uninitialized : !stream.resource<external>{%c4}
  %14 = stream.cmd.execute with(%13 as %arg3: !stream.resource<external>{%c4}) {
    stream.cmd.fill %c1065353216_i32, %arg3[%c0 for %c4] : i32 -> !stream.resource<external>{%c4}
  } => !stream.timepoint
  %15 = stream.timepoint.await %14 => %13 : !stream.resource<external>{%c4}
  %16 = stream.tensor.export %15 : tensor<f32> in !stream.resource<external>{%c4} -> !hal.buffer_view
  return %16 : !hal.buffer_view
}
```

In an async execution mode things are ok but the alloc could stand to be queue-ordered to avoid blocking:
```mlir
func.func @silly(%4: !stream.timepoint, %arg4: !hal.fence) -> !hal.buffer_view {
  %c0 = arith.constant 0 : index
  %c4 = arith.constant 4 : index
  %9 = stream.resource.alloc uninitialized : !stream.resource<external>{%c4}
  %10 = stream.cmd.execute with(%9 as %arg5: !stream.resource<external>{%c4}) {
    stream.cmd.fill %c1065353216_i32, %arg5[%c0 for %c4] : i32 -> !stream.resource<external>{%c4}
  } => !stream.timepoint
  %11 = stream.timepoint.join max(%4, %10) => !stream.timepoint
  stream.timepoint.chain_external %11 => (%arg4 : !hal.fence)
  %16 = stream.tensor.export %9 : tensor<f32> in !stream.resource<external>{%c4} -> !hal.buffer_view
  return %16 : !hal.buffer_view
}
```
